hadiths[13]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27801","Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Abd al-Rahim, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from Yahya ibn al-Husayn, from Umm al-Husayn, his grandmother, she narrated to him, she said: I performed Hajj with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the Farewell Hajj, and I saw Usamah ibn Zayd and Bilal, one of them holding the halter of the she-camel of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and the other lifting his garment shading him from the heat, until he stoned Jamrat al-Aqabah."
"27802","Abu Qatan narrated to us, he said: Yunus, meaning Ibn Abi Ishaq, narrated to us, from al-Ayzar ibn Hurayth, from Umm al-Husayn al-Ahmasiyyah, she said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in the Farewell Hajj delivering a sermon on the minbar, wearing a cloak of his which he had wrapped from under his armpit. She said: I was looking at the muscle of his upper arm quivering, and I heard him say: O people, fear Allah, and even if a mutilated Abyssinian slave is appointed over you, listen to him and obey as long as he upholds among you the Book of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic."
"27803","Waki narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Yahya ibn al-Husayn, from his grandmother, she said: I heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: May Allah have mercy on those who shave, may Allah have mercy on those who shave. They said on the third time: And those who shorten? He said: And those who shorten."
"27804","Waki narrated to us, from Isra'il, from Abu Ishaq, from Yahya ibn al-Husayn, from his mother, she said: I heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, at Arafat delivering a sermon in the Farewell Hajj, saying: O people, fear Allah, and hear and obey, even if a mutilated Abyssinian slave is appointed over you, as long as he upholds among you the Book of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic."
"27805","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Shu'bah, he said: Yahya ibn al-Husayn ibn Urwah narrated to us, he said: My grandmother narrated to me, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Even if a slave is appointed over you leading you by the Book of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, listen to him and obey."
"27806","Rawh narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: I heard Yahya ibn Husayn, he said: I heard my grandmother say: I heard the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, at Arafat delivering a sermon, saying: May Allah forgive those who shave, three times. They said: And those who shorten? So he said on the fourth time: And those who shorten."
"27807","She said: And I heard him say: If a slave is appointed over you leading you by the Book of Allah, listen to him and obey."
"27808","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Yahya ibn al-Husayn, he said: I heard my grandmother narrate that she heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, delivering a sermon in the Farewell Hajj, saying: If a slave is appointed over you leading you by the Book of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, listen to him and obey."
"27809","Waki narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Ayzar ibn Hurayth, from Umm al-Husayn al-Ahmasiyyah, she said: I heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was standing at Arafah, wearing a cloak which he had wrapped himself in, saying: Hear and obey, even if an Abyssinian slave is appointed over you, as long as he upholds among you the Book of Allah."
"27810","Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to me, from Yahya ibn al-Husayn, he said: I heard my grandmother narrate that she heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, at Mina supplicating for those who shave three times. It was said to him: And those who shorten? So he said on the third time: And those who shorten."
"27811","Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, he said: Yunus narrated to us, from al-Ayzar ibn Hurayth, he said: I heard Umm al-Husayn al-Ahmasiyyah say: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in the Farewell Hajj, wearing a cloak which he had wrapped from under his armpit, and I was looking at the muscle of his upper arm quivering, while he was saying: O people, fear Allah and obey, and even if a mutilated Abyssinian slave is appointed over you, hear and obey as long as he upholds among you the Book of Allah."
"27812","Affan narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn al-Husayn narrated to us, he informed me that he heard his grandmother say: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, delivering a sermon at Arafat, saying: Even if a slave is appointed over you leading you by the Book of Allah, listen to him and obey. Abdullah said: And I heard my father say: I consider hearing and obeying him due in hardship and ease, in activity and dislike."
"27813","Waki narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah said: I came to Yahya ibn al-Husayn and asked him, and he said: My grandmother narrated to me, she said: I heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying while he was standing at Arafah: If an Abyssinian slave is appointed over you, listen to him and obey as long as he leads you by the Book of Allah, the Exalted."
